<title>CANADA: Canada auto union to strike if deadline passes.</title>
<headline>Canada auto union to strike if deadline passes.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Auto Workers union president Buzz Hargrove said on Tuesday that if negotiations with Chrysler Corp's Canadian unit are not concluded by Tuesday's midnight deadline, union members will go on strike until a deal is ratified on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;When we have a strike we do not return to work until there is a ratification,&quot; Hargrove said.</p>
<p>He said the earliest a tentative agreement could be ratified by the union membership would be on Sunday.</p>
<p>&quot;We have meetings scheduled for Saturday and Sunday,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
</text>
